  {
   "what": "Journey spread at n>=5",
   "why": "journey capped at n=3 rounds per variant (coordinator instruction, host contention made each round slow); medians with min/max over 3 runs"
  },
  {
   "what": "App Store thinned / compressed download size",
   "why": "no signing identity or App Store Connect; reported the unsigned device-arch (arm64) .app plus an IPA-shaped zip instead"
  },
  {
   "what": "Device (iPhone) numbers",
   "why": "simulator only by instruction: CPU and memory are the Mac's host process, network is loopback"
  },
  {
   "what": "Tap/interaction capture cost",
   "why": "the journey is timer-driven inside the app (no synthesised touches), so neither SDK's tap tracking ran"
  },
  {
   "what": "Init time for base",
   "why": "no SDK call to time (baseline)"
  },
  {
   "what": "Host load for the first init launches",
   "why": "the load logger was added part-way through the init phase (coordinator request); those launches have load1 null"
  },
  {
   "what": "Work done for the app by other processes (backboardd, render server, simulator networking)",
   "why": "proc_pid_rusage counts the app process only"
  }
 ],
 "method": "See README.md. One app, one source, three Release builds (base / OuoSDK / sentry-cocoa); replay is a runtime switch on the same binary. Size: device build (generic/platform=iOS, arm64, unsigned then ad-hoc signed), .app bytes and IPA-shaped zip (deflate 9); deltas vs base. Init: DispatchTime around Ouo.start / SentrySDK.start in didFinishLaunching, main thread, 12 cold launches on fresh installs per variant. CPU/memory: proc_pid_rusage(RUSAGE_INFO_V6) every 0.5 s on the simulator app's host PID (user+system CPU, phys_footprint); idle window 5-20 s (memory 10-20 s), journey window 20-80 s, peak 0-85 s. Wire: local capture server answering 200 itself, request body bytes as sent (gzip) for every SDK request from launch to 100 s (85 s foreground, 15 s background), scaled to per minute. 3 journey rounds per variant (n=3, cut from the planned 6 for run time under host contention), interleaved and rotated. Timer-driven journey (no synthesised taps). Simulator numbers: host CPU and memory, loopback network. Host was heavily loaded (1-min load ~10-30 on 10 cores, a parallel Android emulator run); variants interleaved and rotated per round so both SDKs saw the same contention; host load average logged every 5 s and attached per run (load1).",
